===Verb===
{{en-verb|pan<> and scan<>}}

# {{lb|en|film}} To adjust widescreen film images so that they can be shown with standard television aspect ratios by cropping the original image, i.e. using pan and scan methods.
# {{lb|en|film}} To crop out (a character or object) when performing the pan and scan process, resulting in the deletion of a character or object.
#: {{ux|en|In the full-screen version of Star Wars Episode II, only Anakin and Obi-Wan appear in the scene because Padmé was '''panned and scanned''' out.}}

